## 🚀 How to Contribute

### 1. Set Up Your Local Environment

1. **Fork the Repository** on GitHub.
2. **Clone your fork** locally:
   ```bash
   git clone [https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPOSITORY-NAME.git](https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPOSITORY-NAME.git)
   cd YOUR-REPOSITORY-NAME
Create a topic branch:

Bash
git checkout -b feature/add-new-command
2. Adding a New Command
To add a new command to the agent, update the decision router inside main.py:

Python
# 1. Add your keyword handling condition
elif "weather" in cmd:
    return "Weather module is running offline. Current status: Clear skies."
3. Commit Guidelines
Please use clear Conventional Commit messages:

feat: A new feature or command handler (e.g., feat: add status command handler).

fix: A bug fix or syntax correction (e.g., fix: strip trailing spaces on input).

docs: Documentation changes only (e.g., docs: update command table in README).

refactor: Code restructuring without changing behavior.

4. Submitting a Pull Request (PR)
Push your branch to GitHub:

Bash
git push origin feature/add-new-command
Open a Pull Request against the main branch.

Ensure your PR description clearly states:

What command or fix was added.

Steps to test the change in the terminal loop.
